            <ArticleTitle>Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma presenting as median nerve compression in the arm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 70-year-old woman presented with median nerve compression secondary to enlarged supratrochlear lymph nodes infiltrated with malignant non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. Peripheral nerve compression is rarely seen in this condition. The management and prognosis are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
